.TH mouser-default-terminal 1  "mouser-default-terminal 1.4.5" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mouser\-default\-terminal \- Windows: make Mouser the default terminal for console programs (docs/windows.md §Default terminal). Needs Windows Terminal installed
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser default\-terminal\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Windows: make Mouser the default terminal for console programs (docs/windows.md §Default terminal). Needs Windows Terminal installed
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mouser\-default\-terminal\-status(1)
Whether Mouser is registered and what the default terminal is
.TP
mouser\-default\-terminal\-register(1)
Register Mouser\*(Aqs handoff for this user (the installer does this; the default is unchanged)
.TP
mouser\-default\-terminal\-unregister(1)
Remove Mouser\*(Aqs handoff (and put back the previous default if Mouser is it)
.TP
mouser\-default\-terminal\-set(1)
Make Mouser the default terminal, remembering the current one
.TP
mouser\-default\-terminal\-unset(1)
Put back the default terminal from before `set`
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmouser\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v1.4.5
